]prompts/202610/unblock_e2_release_cutover.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1oe[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1oe/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]release.yml finds the previous release in a throwaway venv and[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]fails loudly on real errors[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]resolver[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]resolver: release.yml's previous-release resolver moves into [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tools/exercise_release, dry-runs each candidate in a throwaway uv venv [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]instead of the externally managed --system interpreter, shows uv's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stderr, and stops on errors that are not resolution failures. The SC2012[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dist counts in the build step are replaced too.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]A failed core cut stops counting as red once a newer cut [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]succeeds[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]cut-red[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cut-red: in sase-core, handle_no_train reports CoreCutRed only when the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]newest decisive completed cut is a typed failure. A later successful cut[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]supersedes a stale red cut. Rust state tests and the steward state docs [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]row are updated.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Master pins the published core that contains its source [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]revision[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-pin[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cut-red[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-pin: once a complete published sase-core-rs (expected 0.42.7) [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]contains sase-core-revision.txt, ratchet master's exact pin and uv.lock [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]to it. If that tag also carries the cut-red fix, move the revision pin [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]to the tag commit so the steward builds the fixed policy.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Prove a green master rehearsal, then raise a handover gate [/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]that really executes[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]cutover[dim] · [dim][/dim]after resolver, core-pin[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cutover: prove a green master rehearsal of release.yml and a steward [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]verdict past every core check, write corrected handover notes on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-1n6.10 and sase-1n6, close this phase, then raise one gate whose [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]options flip merge authority and the tag-only pypi rule and relaunch [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-1n6.10 fresh.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-1oe","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-1oe.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-256bb38cc5f7ed3997106ed38e3f99db","started_at":"2026-10-26T12:43:33.237289+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[{"committed_at":1793061099,"sha":"816efdc9d755fc26e8f832956b0ec8936c180213","subject":"chore(core): ratchet sase-core-rs pin to published 0.42.7"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"15475d00a851baf7b765a5ed6bfae06e7e0423622bec4a7d9a15200114522d24","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1oe.3--3/chat.md","size_bytes":41229},"commits":{"digest":"bc14bc4d37f9351f5ab5b813ee88830e0686755d7aefa1aa1463d0d87a7ab88c","path":"agents